From 54922a2e1279ed514fcfaeba770721d540b9a998 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mstsc-wine <mstsc-wine@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:33:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 44/45] winex11: Match national characters to the layout tables
 in a UTF-8 locale.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

X11DRV_KEYBOARD_DetectLayout() and X11DRV_InitKeyboard() both convert the
keysyms of a keycode to single bytes to compare them with the layout tables,
which are encoded in Latin-1 (or KOI8 and similar). When XkbTranslateKeySym()
cannot express a keysym in one byte, as in any UTF-8 locale for every
non-ASCII character, DetectLayout() falls back to the low byte of the keysym,
but InitKeyboard() replaced it with 0.

The layout was therefore detected correctly, but the keys with national
characters (for instance ü, ö, ä and ß on a German keyboard) never matched
their table entries. They got spare virtual keys and arbitrary scancodes from
0x60 on instead of the scancodes of their positions, so applications that
forward scancodes, such as terminal-services clients, sent the wrong keys.

Use the same fallback in both places.
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c
index 25836fe8..c291e6e2 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/keyboard.c
@@ -1662,8 +1662,11 @@ void X11DRV_InitKeyboard( Display *display )
                         /* FIXME: query what keysym is used as Mode_switch, fill XKeyEvent
                          * with appropriate ShiftMask and Mode_switch, use XLookupString
                          * to get character in the local encoding.
+                         * Use the same fallback as X11DRV_KEYBOARD_DetectLayout, so that
+                         * national characters (for instance in a UTF-8 locale, where
+                         * they do not fit in one byte) still match the layout tables.
                          */
-                        ckey[i] = (keysym <= 0x7F) ? keysym : 0;
+                        ckey[i] = keysym & 0xFF;
                     }
 		} else {
 		  ckey[i] = KEYBOARD_MapDeadKeysym(keysym);
-- 
